WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:05.640
With ArtiosCAD
you can easily design your packaging,

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.680
view and present the result in 3D

00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:11.200
and prepare for production
in a minimum amount of time.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.400
ArtiosCAD is the world's most popular
Structural Design application

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:16.640
for packaging.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.640
In this sequence we will show you
how fast you can design any packaging

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.000
within minutes with ArtiosCAD.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:27.960
ArtiosCAD has a huge library
of parametric designs.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.400
We call them standards.

00:00:29.560 --> 00:00:32.680
Based on material thickness
and basic internal dimensions,

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:34.560
length, width and depth,

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.400
you're able to create
a standard carton in seconds.

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:40.280
Layers with dimensions
are created automatically.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.280
You can modify values or make
specific style choices at the start

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.640
or at a later stage of design.

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.800
As you can see,
all subsequent values are updated.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:53.720
Bleed and varnish areas can be added
in only a few mouse clicks.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.560
You can import graphics
into ArtiosCAD as well.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:00.960
To ensure consistency
we convert the design to 3D.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:05.120
3D visualization allows you
to do a visual check of your design.

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.520
Creating virtual mock-ups instead of
physical samples saves time and money

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.080
and you obtain
a faster customer approval.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.680
The finished design
will need to be output,

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:20.000
in this case to a spec sheet, which
may contain both 2D and 3D elements

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.680
and can be completed with
a range of design-related information.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:26.600
In this example,
we export the report as a PDF

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:28.960
in which
the 3D view is still interactive,

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:31.880
so the customer can view
the design from all angles.

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:36.040
To cut some live samples we can choose
one of the many preset outputs

00:01:36.200 --> 00:01:39.400
to plotter tables,
like a Kongsberg Digital Cutting Table.

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:42.200
Before output, we can even
check the sequence of data

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.880
that ArtiosCAD will transfer
to the cutting table.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.840
This will ensure
optimal performance and sample quality.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.160
Finally, when the design is approved,
we make a sheet lay-out.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:56.920
Lay-outs are based on the maximum
and minimum sizes of your presses,

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:59.760
so you end up with the optimum number
of designs on a sheet

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:02.480
and the minimum amount
of material waste.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:05.920
This file is the starting point
for the production of printing plates

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.400
and of the corresponding dieboard.

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:11.880
You can also generate coating blankets
from this sheet lay-out.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.640
Accelerate your packaging design
with ArtiosCAD

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.360
and prepare for production
in a minimum amount of time.

